      "content": "The score on that last one was definitely higher, though it felt a little clunky with the phrasing. \n\nJust a heads up: the marketing leads are actually getting a bit picky. They specifically said they don't want the text to feel like a \"list of keywords\" or to be \"hollow/repetitive.\" They want the lore to feel natural, even if the score goes up. Please don't just keyword-stuff or pad the text just to chase the metric—the quality of the writing is still the most important thing, the score is just a guide.\n\nLet's do one more to see if we can find that sweet spot. The item is: **\"A Faded Silk Ribbon\"**",
